  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A feature I’d like to suggest interfacing with the Trust system is the ability for VRChat to detect if your shader has Cull Off, and to flag that option on fallback shaders. \n\nI frequently use single-sided meshes when modeling to reduce poly count and create the illusion of, say, an inside of a jacket, without actually extruding the polys. This is a common optimization technique in the industry and the fact that the VRChat fallback shaders have culling on by default means any models created that rely on double sided shaders have parts that appear invisible from one side when the user that uploaded the avatar is not Trusted or a Friend.\n\nI would greatly appreciate a system that modifies the fallback shader to match the culling mode of the uploaded shader.\n\nThanks,\nCheers.",
